  "story": {
    "premise": "The evacuation controller will no longer obey one writer merely because it repeats itself. Station operations, traffic control, and the clinic each send an attestation for the last-train release. Trigger once, immediately after any two distinct sources have spoken, and retain the exact payload of the attestation that completed the quorum.",
    "submission": "Submit a canonical PULSE 0.1 program and, optionally, a short invariant. The release is one-shot, has zero added latency, and must carry the canonical payload of the second distinct source event.",
    "diagnostics": "The verifier exhausts all 3,478 source-tagged streams of up to four votes over four ticks. It distinguishes duplicate votes, delayed two-source agreement, all-three same-tick EventId order, wrong decisive payloads, and repeated release.",
    "hints": ["Three monotone seen bits are enough; a retry sets an already-true bit.", "After marking the current source, ask whether either other source has already appeared.", "Seal the controller when it emits. The third source is evidence, not a second command."]
